  <h2>The independence line matters operationally</h2>
  <p>
    Kakobuy.net&apos;s own copy stresses that it is <strong>not officially affiliated</strong> with Kakobuy.com, does <strong>not</strong> process checkouts as the merchant of record, and exists to <strong>educate and route discovery</strong>.
    That is the same structural separation we use across this hub: <strong>editorial and curator layers</strong> are not your wallet, QC console, or customs declaration form.
    If a page feels &quot;official,&quot; verify the registrant and the checkout domain before you assign blame for fees or delays.
  </p>

  <h2>Two different meanings of &quot;QC&quot;</h2>
  <p>
    Finds hubs often show <strong>representative inspection photos</strong>—useful for narrowing candidates quickly. Kakobuy&apos;s operational QC is tied to <strong>your SKUs arriving at their warehouse</strong>, with timing and angles governed by warehouse workflows—not by whichever JPEG impressed you on a catalogue row.
    Treat catalogue QC as <strong>research signal</strong>; treat signed-in warehouse albums as <strong>accept/reject evidence</strong>. Our <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">Spreadsheet QC essay</a> stays the authoritative framing here.
  </p>

